    "background_story": "Emir was a charismatic food cart vendor in the bustling streets of Istanbul. His claim to fame was his mouthwatering polony sandwiches, made with thinly sliced meats and spices that danced on the taste buds. Emir's passion for polony was inspired by his grandfather, a skilled butcher who had perfected the recipe. Every morning, Emir would carefully select the finest ingredients and cook the polony to perfection, filling the air with its irresistible aroma. As the day went on, his cart would attract a loyal following of locals and tourists alike, all drawn in by the tantalizing flavors and Emir's warm hospitality. Despite the rise of trendy eateries, Emir's humble cart remained a beloved institution, thanks to his dedication to traditional flavors and his warm, welcoming smile.",
